-- title:
--   Claim 3.2: rank-$r$ elements of $\langle T\rangle$ meet at most $(1+|T|+N|T|^2)^{2^{d+2}}$ classes
-- statement:
--   Let $d$ be a positive integer, $X\subseteq\mathrm{Mat}_d(\mathbb Q)$ finite and nonempty, $\sim$ a congruence on $\langle X\rangle$ and $N\ge1$ such that every stable subsemigroup $S\le\langle X\rangle$ satisfies $|S/\sim|\le N$. Let $T\subseteq\langle X\rangle$ be finite and let all matrices of $T$ have rank $r$. Then the rank-$r$ matrices in the semigroup $\langle T\rangle$ generated by $T$ meet at most
--   $$(1+|T|+N|T|^2)^{2^{d+2}}$$
--   classes of $\langle X\rangle/\sim$.
--
--   This is the counting step of the induction in the proof of Theorem 1: it bounds the classes of rank-preserving products over a fixed finite set of representatives.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The number of classes is a `Set.encard`, so the bound includes finiteness.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: "the rank-r matrices in ⟨T⟩ meet at most … congruence classes" → `Set.encard` of the classes of ⟨X⟩/∼ containing an element of `Subsemigroup.closure T` of rank r; reason: the same count, in ℕ ∪ {∞}
-- source:
--   Guttenberg, Lhote, Shirmohammadi, Worrell, Burnside Problems for Matrix Semigroup Quotients with Applications to Border Complexity, STOC 2027 submission (held version, sha256 1bc61d4e…), Appendix B, Claim 3.2, p.30 (also p.9), with the standing assumption of Appendix B, p.29

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MatSemiBurnside_classesMeeting
set_option autoImplicit false

namespace MatSemiBurnside

/-- **Claim 3.2.** Guttenberg, Lhote, Shirmohammadi, Worrell, *Burnside Problems for Matrix Semigroup Quotients
with Applications to Border Complexity*, STOC 2027 submission (held version, sha256 1bc61d4e…), Appendix B, Claim 3.2, p.30 (also p.9), under the standing assumption of
Appendix B, p.29 ("Fix a finite nonempty set X ⊆ Matd(ℚ) and a congruence ∼ on ⟨X⟩. For the two
claims below, assume that every stable subsemigroup S ≤ ⟨X⟩ satisfies |S/∼| ≤ N."): "Let T ⊆ ⟨X⟩ be
finite and all its matrices have rank r. The rank-r matrices in ⟨T⟩ meet at most
(1 + |T| + N|T|²)^(2^(d+2)) congruence classes."

**Formalization Note.** N is the positive integer of Theorem 1. ⟨T⟩ is `Subsemigroup.closure T`;
the classes counted are classes of ⟨X⟩/∼ met by the rank-r elements of ⟨T⟩, counted by
`Set.encard` (so the bound includes finiteness). -/
theorem claim_3_2 {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d) (X : Finset (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℚ)) (hX : X.Nonempty)
    (c : Con (Subsemigroup.closure (X : Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℚ)))) (N : ℕ) (hN : 1 ≤ N) (hbound : UniformStableBound X c N)
    (T : Finset (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℚ)) (hT : (T : Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℚ)) ⊆ Subsemigroup.closure (X : Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℚ)))
    (r : ℕ) (hTr : ∀ a ∈ T, a.rank = r) :
    (classesMeeting c {a | a ∈ Subsemigroup.closure (T : Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℚ)) ∧ a.rank = r}).encard ≤
      (((1 + T.card + N * T.card ^ 2) ^ (2 ^ (d + 2)) : ℕ) : ℕ∞) := by sorry

end MatSemiBurnside
